msgstr "int **gaussian** = 2"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:357
msgid "Noise Functions"
msgstr "Ruis functies"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:360
msgid "float **cellnoise** ( vector v )"
msgstr "float **cellnoise** ( vector v )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:361
msgid "float **cellnoise1** ( float x )"
msgstr "float **cellnoise1** ( float x )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:362
msgid "float **cellnoise2** ( float x, float y )"
msgstr "float **cellnoise2** ( float x, float y )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:363
msgid "float **cellnoise3** ( float x, float y, float z )"
msgstr "float **cellnoise3** ( float x, float y, float z )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:364
msgid "color **ccellnoise** ( vector v )"
msgstr "color **ccellnoise** ( vector v )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:366
msgid ""
"``cellnoise`` generates a field of constant colored cubes based on the "
"integer location. This is the same as the `PRMan cellnoise function <https://"
"renderman.pixar.com/resources/RenderMan_20/cellnoise.html>`_."
msgstr ""
"``cellnoise`` genereert een veld van constant gekleurde kubussen op basis "
"van de locatie van het gehele getal. Dit is gelijk aan de `PRMan cellnoise "
"function <https://renderman.pixar.com/resources/RenderMan_20/cellnoise."
"html>`_."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:370
msgid "``ccellnoise`` outputs color cellnoise."
msgstr "``ccellnoise`` geeft gekleurde cell-ruis."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:372
msgid ""
"float **fbm** ( vector v, int octaves=6, float lacunarity=2, float gain=0.5 )"
msgstr ""
"float **fbm** ( vector v, int octaves=6, float lacunarity=2, float gain=0.5 )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:373
msgid ""
"color **cfbm** ( vector v, int octaves=6, float lacunarity=2, float "
"gain=0.5 )"
msgstr ""
"color **cfbm** ( vector v, int octaves=6, float lacunarity=2, float "
"gain=0.5 )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:374
msgid ""
"vector **vfbm** ( vector v, int octaves=6, float lacunarity=2, float "
"gain=0.5 )"
msgstr ""
"vector **vfbm** ( vector v, int octaves=6, float lacunarity=2, float "
"gain=0.5 )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:375
msgid ""
"float **fbm4** ( vector v, float time, int octaves=6, float lacunarity=2, "
"float gain=0.5 )"
msgstr ""
"float **fbm4** ( vector v, float time, int octaves=6, float lacunarity=2, "
"float gain=0.5 )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:376
msgid ""
"color **cfbm4** ( vector v, float time, int octaves=6, float lacunarity=2, "
"float gain=0.5 )"
msgstr ""
"color **cfbm4** ( vector v, float time, int octaves=6, float lacunarity=2, "
"float gain=0.5 )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:377
msgid ""
"vector **vfbm4** ( vector v, float time, int octaves=6, float lacunarity=2, "
"float gain=0.5 )"
msgstr ""
"vector **vfbm4** ( vector v, float time, int octaves=6, float lacunarity=2, "
"float gain=0.5 )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:379
msgid ""
"``fbm`` (Fractal Brownian Motion) is a multi-frequency noise function. The "
"base frequency is the same as the ``noise`` function. The total number of "
"frequencies is controlled by ``octaves``. The ``lacunarity`` is the spacing "
"between the frequencies - a value of 2 means each octave is twice the "
"previous frequency. The ``gain`` controls how much each frequency is scaled "
"relative to the previous frequency."
msgstr ""
"``fbm`` (Fractale Brownse beweging) is een multi-frequentie ruis functie. De "
"basis frequentie is gelijk aan de ``noise`` (ruis)functie. Het totale aantal "
"frequenties wordt geregeld met ``octaves``. The ``lacunariteit`` regelt de "
"afstand tussen de frequenties - een waarde 2 betekent dat elke octaaf twee "
"keer de voorgaande frequentie is. De ``gain` regelt de schaal van elke "
"frequentie vergeleken met die van de vorige frequentie."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:388
msgid "``cfbm`` and ``cfbm4`` outputs color noise."
msgstr "``cfbm`` en ``cfbm4`` geeft gekleurde ruis."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:390
msgid "``vfbm`` and ``vfbm4`` outputs vector noise."
msgstr "``vfbm`` en ``vfbm4`` geeft vector ruis."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:391
msgid "float **hash** ( float seed1, [float seed2, ...] )"
msgstr "float **hash** ( float seed1, [float seed2, ...] )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:393
msgid ""
"Like ``rand``, but with no internal seeds. Any number of seeds may be given "
"and the result will be a random function based on all the seeds."
msgstr ""
"Als ``rand``, maar zonder interne seeds. Elk aantal seeds is mogelijk en het "
"gegeven antwoord  is afhankelijk van alle gegeven seeds."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:396
msgid "float **noise** ( vector v )"
msgstr "float **noise** ( vector v )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:397
msgid "float **noise** ( float x, float y )"
msgstr "float **noise** ( float x, float y )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:398
msgid "float **noise** ( float x, float y, float z )"
msgstr "float **noise** ( float x, float y, float z )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:399
msgid "float **noise** ( float x, float y, float z, float w )"
msgstr "float **noise** ( float x, float y, float z, float w )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:400
msgid "color **cnoise** ( vector v)"
msgstr "color **cnoise** ( vector v)"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:401
msgid "color **cnoise4** ( vector v, float t)"
msgstr "color **cnoise4** ( vector v, float t)"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:402
msgid "float **pnoise** ( vector v, vector period )"
msgstr "float **pnoise** ( vector v, vector period )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:403
msgid "float **snoise** ( vector v)"
msgstr "float **snoise** ( vector v)"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:404
msgid "float **snoise4** ( vector v, float t)"
msgstr "float **snoise4** ( vector v, float t)"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:405
msgid "vector **vnoise** (vector v )"
msgstr "vector **vnoise** (vector v )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:406
msgid "vector **vnoise4** (vector v, float t )"
msgstr "vector **vnoise4** (vector v, float t )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:408
msgid ""
"``noise`` is a random function that smoothly blends between samples at "
"integer locations. This is Ken Perlin's original noise function."
msgstr ""
"``noise`` is een functie voor willekeurigheid die soepel mengt tussen "
"samples op locaties met gehele getallen. Dit is de originele noise-functie "
"van Ken Perlin."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:413
msgid "``cnoise`` and ``cnoise4`` output color noise."
msgstr "``cnoise`` en ``cnoise4`` geven gekleurde ruis."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:415
msgid "``noise4`` outputs signed vector noise."
msgstr "``noise4`` geeft van teken voorziene vector-noise."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:417
msgid "``pnoise`` outputs periodic noise."
msgstr "``pnoise`` geeft periodieke ruis."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:419
msgid "``snoise`` and ``snoise4`` output signed noise with range ``[-1, 1]``."
msgstr ""
"``snoise`` en ``snoise4`` geeft noise (ruis) met een teken binnen de reeks "
"``[-1, 1]``."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:421
msgid "``vnoise`` outputs signed vector noise."
msgstr "``vnoise`` geeft van teken voorziene vector-noise."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:422
msgid "float **rand** ( [float min, float max], [float seed] )"
msgstr "float **rand** ( [float min, float max], [float seed] )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:424
msgid ""
"Random number between ``[min, max]`` (or ``[0, 1]`` if unspecified). If a "
"seed is supplied, it will be used in addition to the internal seeds and may "
"be used to create multiple distinct generators."
msgstr ""
"Willekeurig getal tussen ``[min, max]`` (of ``[0, 1]`` indien niet "
"gespecificeerd). Als een seed is gegeven, zal het gebruikt worden naast de "
"interne seeds en kan gebruikt worden om meerdere gescheiden generators aan "
"te maken."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:427
msgid ""
"float **turbulence** ( vector v, int octaves=6, float lacunarity=2, float "
"gain=0.5 )"
msgstr ""
"float **turbulence** ( vector v, int octaves=6, float lacunarity=2, float "
"gain=0.5 )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:428
msgid ""
"color **cturbulence** ( vector v, int octaves=6, float lacunarity=2, float "
"gain=0.5 )"
msgstr ""
"color **cturbulence** ( vector v, int octaves=6, float lacunarity=2, float "
"gain=0.5 )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:429
msgid ""
"vector **vturbulence** ( vector v, int octaves=6, float lacunarity=2, float "
"gain=0.5 )"
msgstr ""
"vector **vturbulence** ( vector v, int octaves=6, float lacunarity=2, float "
"gain=0.5 )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:431
msgid ""
"``turbulence`` is a variant of ``fbm`` where the absolute value of each "
"noise term is taken. This gives a more billowy appearance."
msgstr ""
"``turbulence`` is een variant van ``fbm`` waar de absolute waarde van elke "
"ruisterm is genomen. Ziet er meer golvend uit."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:433
msgid ""
"float **voronoi** ( vector v, int type=1, float jitter=0.5, float "
"fbmScale=0, int fbmOctaves=4, float fbmLacunarity=2, float fbmGain=0.5)"
msgstr ""
"float **voronoi** ( vector v, int type=1, float jitter=0.5, float "
"fbmScale=0, int fbmOctaves=4, float fbmLacunarity=2, float fbmGain=0.5)"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:434
msgid ""
"color **cvoronoi** ( vector v, int type=1, float jitter=0.5, float "
"fbmScale=0, int fbmOctaves=4, float fbmLacunarity=2, float fbmGain=0.5)"
msgstr ""
"color **cvoronoi** ( vector v, int type=1, float jitter=0.5, float "
"fbmScale=0, int fbmOctaves=4, float fbmLacunarity=2, float fbmGain=0.5)"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:435
msgid ""
"vector **pvoronoi** ( vector v, float jitter=0.5, float fbmScale=0, int "
"fbmOctaves=4, float fbmLacunarity=2, float fbmGain=0.5)"
msgstr ""
"vector **pvoronoi** ( vector v, float jitter=0.5, float fbmScale=0, int "
"fbmOctaves=4, float fbmLacunarity=2, float fbmGain=0.5)"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:437
msgid ""
"``voronoi`` is a cellular noise pattern. It is a jittered variant of "
"``cellnoise``. The type parameter describes different variants of the noise "
"function. The ``jitter`` param controls how irregular the pattern is (0 is "
"like ordinary cellnoise). The ``fbm...`` params can be used to distort the "
"noise field. When ``fbmScale`` is zero (the default), there is no "
"distortion. The remaining params are the same as for the ``fbm`` function."
msgstr ""
"``voronoi`` is een cellulair ruispatroon. Het is een zenuwachtige variant "
"van ``cellnoise``. Het type parameter beschrijft verschillende varianten van "
"de ruisfunctie. De parameter ``jitter`` bestuurt hoe onregelmatig het "
"patroon is (0 is zoals gewone cellnoise er uit ziet). De parameters ``fbm..."
"`` kunnen gebruikt worden om het ruisveld te verstoren. Wanneer ``fbmScale`` "
"nul is (de standaard), is er geen verstoring. De overblijvende parameters "
"zijn hetzelfde als voor de functie ``fbm``."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:448
msgid "Voronoi types 1 through 5:"
msgstr "Voronoi types 1 tot 5:"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:450
msgid "|image0| |image1| |image2| |image3| |image4|"
msgstr "|image0| |image1| |image2| |image3| |image4|"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:453
msgid ""
"``cvoronoi`` returns a random color for each cell and ``pvoronoi`` returns "
"the point location of the center of the cell."
msgstr ""
"``cvoronoi`` geeft een willekeurige kleur voor elk vakje en ``pvoronoi`` "
"geeft de punt-locatie voor het middelpunt van dat vakje."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:459
msgid "Selection Functions"
msgstr "Functies voor selectie"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:462
msgid "float **choose** ( float index, float choice1, float choice2, [...] )"
msgstr "float **choose** ( float index, float choice1, float choice2, [...] )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:464
msgid ""
"Chooses one of the supplied choices based on the index (assumed to be in the "
"range ``[0, 1]``)."
msgstr ""
"Selecteert een van de in de index opgegeven keuzes (aangenomen dat die in de "
"range vallen ``[0, 1]``)."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:466
msgid "int **cycle** ( int index, int loRange, int hiRange )"
msgstr "int **cycle** ( int index, int loRange, int hiRange )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:468
msgid ""
"Cycles through values between loRange and hiRange based on supplied index. "
"This is an offset ``mod`` function. The result is computed as ``loRange + "
"value % (hiRange-loRange+1)``."
msgstr ""
"Cyclisch gaan door de waarden tussen loRange en hiRange, op basis van de "
"gegeven index. Dit is een offset ``mod``-functie. Het resultaat wordt "
"berekend als ``loRange + value % (hiRange-loRange+1)``."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:471
msgid ""
"int **pick** ( float index, int loRange, int hiRange, [ float "
"weights, ... ] )"
msgstr ""
"int **pick** ( float index, int loRange, int hiRange, [ float "
"weights, ... ] )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:473
msgid ""
"Picks values randomly between loRange and hiRange based on supplied index "
"(which is automatically hashed). The values will be distributed according to "
"the supplied weights. Any weights not supplied are assumed to be 1.0."
msgstr ""
"Kiest willekeurige waarden tussen loRange en hiRange op basis van de "
"opgegeven index (met automatische hash). De waarden worden verdeeld volgens "
"de opgegeven gewichten. Een niet opgegeven gewicht wordt verondersteld 1.0 "
"te zijn."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:477
msgid ""
"float **wchoose** ( float index, float choice1, float weight1, float "
"choice2, float weight2, [...] )"
msgstr ""
"float **wchoose** ( float index, float choice1, float weight1, float "
"choice2, float weight2, [...] )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:479
msgid ""
"Chooses one of the supplied choices based on the index (assumed to be in "
"range ``[0, 1]``). The values will be distributed according to the supplied "
"weights."
msgstr ""
"Kiest een van de opgegeven keuzes op basis van de index (volgens aanname in "
"bereik ``[0, 1]``. De waarden worden verdeeld naar de opgegeven gewichten."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:485
msgid "This example returns integer values between 1 and 10::"
msgstr "Dit voorbeeld geeft gehele getallen tussen 1 en 10::"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:487
msgid "pick(value, 1, 10)"
msgstr "pick(value, 1, 10)"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:489
msgid ""
"This example returns the values 1 and 2 twice and 2.5 times as often "
